course: dictionary
lesson: 12745
title: Dual, meaning two
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dual means having two parts, uses or sides. Look for clue words in the sentence, such as two, both or at the same time. «The new road is a dual carriageway with two lanes going each way.» Two lanes each way tells you dual means having two of something.
explain: «Maya has dual citizenship, so she is a citizen of two countries at the same time.» The words at the same time help you see that dual means both at once. Try the swap: double fits here too, so dual is close in meaning to double.
explain: Dual is often used in phrases. «The shed has a dual purpose: it is a garage and a workshop.» Purpose means use, so a dual purpose is two uses. Other common partners are dual controls, dual-language and dual citizenship.
explain: In maths, dual can mean a matching partner. A cube and an octahedron are duals of each other, each matching the other in a special way. Dual is a word that often comes with a clear picture of two, so look for that picture first.
fact: Dual means having two parts, uses or sides; it is a double.
fact: «Dual carriageway» means a road with two lanes in each direction.
fact: «Dual citizenship» means being a citizen of two countries at the same time.
fact: «Dual-language» books have two languages on the page, such as English and Welsh.
fact: In maths, a cube and an octahedron are duals: each one is a matching partner of the other.
exercise: «The new road is a dual carriageway with two lanes each way.» What does dual mean here? | *Having two parts, with two lanes each way | Very fast and smooth | A road with no lanes at all | Built out of stone
exercise: «Maya has dual citizenship: she is a citizen of Britain and India at the same time.» How many countries is Maya a citizen of? | Three | One | None | *Two
exercise: «The book is dual-language, with English and Welsh on each page.» What does dual-language mean? | A very old language | A language for animals | *Two languages | Only one language
test: A learner car has dual controls, so the instructor can use a second pedal. What does dual mean here? | Very fast | *Two of something, a second set | Painted red | Broken and unsafe
test: Jo says a cube and an octahedron are duals. In maths, what does this mean? | They never match in any way | They have no corners | *They are matching partners | They are both wet
exam: Which phrase means a road with two lanes in each direction? | *dual carriageway | dual citizenship | dual purpose | dual-language
